# Ruby ships json and net-imap as DEFAULT gems; the toolchain image's ruby
# (4.0.4) bundles json 2.18.0 / net-imap 0.6.2 under /mise/installs/ruby. The
# app does NOT load those — it runs the patched vendored copies pinned in
# backend/Gemfile.lock (json 2.19.5, net-imap 0.6.4) under BUNDLE_DEPLOYMENT.
# The default gemspecs are dormant files, but the scanner still flags them.
# Remove these once the ruby toolchain ships fixed defaults. Tracked in #485.
CVE-2026-33210
CVE-2026-42245
CVE-2026-42246
CVE-2026-42257
CVE-2026-42258

# Transitive deps compiled into third-party binaries we don't author. No fix
# in a released Caddy / wal-g, so not actionable here — the fix path is an
# upstream release picked up via a Dependabot base-image / WALG_VERSION bump.
# Revisit each when its upstream ships. Tracked in #485.
CVE-2026-34986   # go-jose/v3 in the Caddy (edge) binary — fixed in go-jose 3.0.5
CVE-2026-33816   # jackc/pgx in the wal-g (db) binary — wal-g dep, fixed in pgx 5.9.0
CVE-2026-33186   # google.golang.org/grpc in the wal-g binary — wal-g dep, fixed in grpc 1.79.3
CVE-2021-38599   # wal-g self: false positive — we build v3.0.8 but the binary embeds a v0.0.0 pseudo-version
